	//Events
	
	//Intro event
	
	"Intro.1": "Hello! Come on in.#$b#You must have seen Harvey's letter.",
	"Intro.2": "I wanted to get your patient intake forms filled out sooner rather than later.#$b#When you're running a two-person operation it helps to try and stay organized.",
	"Intro.3": "What he means is it helps me file less paperwork down the line.$h",
	"Intro.4": "Would you like to take a look at the forms?#Actually, I already have a doctor in Zuzu City.#No thanks. I like to live dangerously.",
	"ZuzuAnswer": "Oh, I see. You should stick with them, then: continuity of care is important to maintain whenever possible.",
	"DangerAnswer": "Hm. I wouldn't exactly say that's advisable, but it's ultimately up to you.$s",
	"Intro.6": "He looks kind of... relieved?",
	"Intro.7": "We do also handle prescriptions. Feel free to have yours sent here so you don't have to make the trip into Zuzu City quite so often.",
	"Intro.5": "Just remember, we're here if you ever have an emergency.#$b#Have a good day, @.",
	"Intro.8": "See you later!$h",
	
	//2 Heart Event
	
	"2Hearts.1": "Okay, George. I want you take a deep breath for me.",
	"2Hearts.2": "Mmhmm... and hold it... now breathe out.",
	"2Hearts.3": "Great. Now turn around, please.",
	"2Hearts.4": "How has your breathing been? Any increase in coughing or shortness of breath?",
	"2Hearts.5": "Hmmph... I can breathe just fine. Just because I'm in this chair doesn't mean the rest of me doesn't work!",
	"2Hearts.6": "That's good. My goal is to keep it that way.#$b#I think it would be good for you to try to get out of the house more. Fresh air and exercise will help you stay healthy.",
	"2Hearts.7": "I don't see why I should bother. Fresh air isn't going to make me any less old.",
	"2Hearts.8": "George...$s#$b#Obviously I can't make you do anything, but I do strongly recommend—",
	"2Hearts.9": "Oh!$8#$b#I'm sorry, but you shouldn't be here... these check-ups are supposed to be private.",
	"2Hearts.10": "Not so fast! I'd like to get a second opinion from this ${young man^young lady^youngster}$.",
	"2Hearts.11": "... Alright. If that would make you more comfortable.",
	"2Hearts.12": "What do you think George should do?#He could keep Evelyn company sometimes while she gardens.#He's right. Health always gets worse with age.",
	"GeorgeGood": "That's an excellent idea, @.$h#$b# What do you think, George? Worth a try?",
	"GeorgeBad": "*sigh* Poor health isn't an intrinsic part of being old.$s#$b# It just takes more effort to maintain good health the older you get.",
	"2Hearts.13": "I guess that doesn't sound so bad. Evelyn's always trying to get me outside anyway.",
	"2Hearts.14": "... Well, Evelyn's always trying to get me outside more anyway. I guess I could make the effort.",
	"2Hearts.15": "Thanks for your suggestion, @. I appreciate it.$h#$b#Even if you still really shouldn't be here.",
	"2Hearts.16": "Thank you for your input, @. Now, I really do insist that you leave.",
	"2Hearts.After": "George said he's going to try going out at least once a week when the weather's nice.#$b#It's a great start!$h",
	"2Hearts.After.George": "Hmph. You're lucky you're still young.#$e#You don't have to worry about this kind of thing.",
	"2Hearts.After.Evelyn": "I don't know what you said to him, but thank you for talking to George.#$b#I think he'll like gardening with me more than he wants to admit.",
	
	//4 Heart Event

	"4Hearts.1": "Welcome in!",
	"4Hearts.2": "Just a moment.",
	"4Hearts.3": "Here's your coffee, Dr. Harvey.",
	"4Hearts.4": "Thanks, Gus.",
	"4Hearts.5": "Alright. What can I get for you, @?",
	"4Hearts.6": "#A beer.#A coffee.#A Joja Cola.",
	"4Hearts.7": "You got it! I'll be right back.$h",
	"4Hearts.beer": "It's been a long day, huh?",
	"4Hearts.coffee": "I'd say it's a little late in the day for caffeine, but they do say people in glass houses shouldn't throw stones.",
	"4Hearts.cola": "You're braver than I am, @.#$b#That stuff gives me heart palpitations.",
	"4Hearts.8": "Oh! Not that it's really my business what you're drinking.$8#$b#I apologize. The doctor hat is hard to take off.",
	"4Hearts.9": "#You're not great at conversation starters, huh?#It's fine, I get it.",
	"4Hearts.91": "Ah... not particularly. Is it that obvious?",
	"4Hearts.92": "Well. That's a relief. Still, I need to get better about it.",
	"4Hearts.10": "Anyway, I'm sorry.",
	"4Hearts.11": "Harvey awkwardly turns back to his own drink.",
	"4Hearts.12": "Here you go! Let me know if you need anything else.",
	"4Hearts.13": "#You don't get better at conversations by not having them.#(Say nothing, as a power move)",
	"4Hearts.14": "... I suppose that's true.",
	"4Hearts.15": "So, @... #$b#What did you do before you moved here?",
	"4Hearts.16": "You tell Harvey about your past life in Zuzu City. He tells you about the time he spent there while in medical school.",
	"4Hearts.17": "It looks like you both moved to Stardew Valley in search of a life that was a little less overwhelming...",
	"4Hearts.18": "... Yes, @?",
	"4Hearts.19": "Well, uh... my coffee's gone cold. I ought to get going.",
	
	//6 Heart Event

	"6Hearts.1": "I'm just saying, I don't see why you're so stuck on it in the first place.",
	"6Hearts.2": "Good habits now mean better outcomes later.#$b#At my age you have to start thinking about these things.",
	"6Hearts.3": "This again! Harvey, 'over thirty' is not old. It's not even middle-aged.$3#$b#You don't get to say 'at my age' until you're at least sixty.",
	"6Hearts.4": "I just think I could benefit from more regular, structured exercise. That's all.",
	"6Hearts.5": "So your big plan is to join the aerobics class?$3",
	"6Hearts.6": "The aerobics class that takes place during clinic hours?$3",
	"6Hearts.7": "The aerobics class where basically half the town would be watching you?$3",
	"6Hearts.8": "*Sigh...*",
	"6Hearts.9": "Listen, you're my friend, so I have to be honest: I don't see that working out long-term.",
	"6Hearts.10": "You might have a point...$s",
	"6Hearts.11": "@! Great timing. Back me up here.",
	"6Hearts.12": "Is 'over thirty' old? #No?#Yes?#Is 'old' a bad thing?",
	"6Hearts.no": "See? I'm not the only one who thinks you're being ridiculous.",
	"6Hearts.yes": "Dang it. I shouldn't have asked you to weigh in without context.$s",
	"6Hearts.badthing": "Not at all! Have you seen Linus? I'm pretty sure he could arm wrestle my mom and win.$h#$b#But you try telling that to Harvey. He talks like he's got one foot in the grave.",
	"6Hearts.13": "Maru, don't rope ${him^her^them}$ into this!$7",
	"6Hearts.14": "Okay, okay. Don't get your stethoscope in a twist.",
	"6Hearts.15": "Anyway. Was there something you needed, farmer @?",
	"6Hearts.After": "Please don't tell anyone about that conversation Maru dragged you into.#$b#It's a... sensitive subject.",
	"6Hearts.After.Maru": "I swear, that man loves to invent problems for himself.#$e#He's lucky his best friend is the town's premier problem solver!$h",
		
	//8 Heart Event
	
	"8Hearts.1": "This is Pelican Town, broadcasting on local frequency 140, do you read me?$9",
	"8Hearts.2": "Repeat, do you read me?$9",
	"8Hearts.3": "Pelican Town, this is Blackbird Five Echo Zuzu. Request standard ground report, over.",
	"8Hearts.4": "Someone's there!?$10#$b#Er... I mean!... Blackbird Five Echo Zuzu, standard ground report: Wind at 3 Clicks, 36 Degrees North of West. Temperature at 42 Kraggs. Humidity 53%. Over!$10",
	"8Hearts.5": "Yikes, my pulse is soaring...$7#$b#I didn't expect anyone to actually be using that frequency...",
	"8Hearts.6": "#Are you okay? You look like you saw a ghost.#Sorry, I probably should have knocked first.#Come on, I'm not that scary.",
	"8Hearts.7": "Oh, yes, I'm fine. Just a little rattled.",
	"8Hearts.8": "Yeah, that would have been polite...$s#$b#It's okay. You're not really interrupting anything.",
	"8Hearts.9": "What?#$b#Oh, no, it's not you.",
	"8Hearts.10": "See, I was just fiddling with my radio, flipping through the local frequencies... and I made contact with a real pilot!", 
	"8Hearts.11": "In fact, we can probably see ${him^her^them}$ passing by overhead right now!",
	"8Hearts.12": "Quick, come look!",
	"8Hearts.13": "There!",
	"8Hearts.14": "You know... as a kid, I always dreamed of being a pilot.",
	"8Hearts.15": "...But with my bad eyesight and a petrifying fear of heights, that dream was never going to become a reality.",
	"8Hearts.16": "Oh, don't be sad for me.#$b#I made peace with it a long time ago. The dreams you have as a child aren't always attainable as an adult... that's just the way the world is.#$b#I'm happy listening to the radio chatter from here. We get a lot of civilian air traffic; Stardew Valley is great for scenic flyovers.$h",
	"8Hearts.17": "And anyway, if I was a pilot then I wouldn't be a doctor...#$b#And I wouldn't have moved here to Pelican Town...#$b#And I wouldn't have become friends with you.",
		"R.8Hearts.17": "And anyway, if I was a pilot then I wouldn't be a doctor...#$b#And I wouldn't have moved here to Pelican Town...#$b#And I wouldn't have fallen in love with you.$l",
	"8Hearts.18": "Hey, let me show you my model airplanes.#$b#I have a Blackbird, the same kind that just flew by!$h",
	"8Hearts.19": "For the first time since you met him, Harvey doesn't seem worried about anything.",
	"8Hearts.After1": "I've never told anyone about my interest in aviation or my model planes before...#$b#You're just easy to talk to, I guess.",
		"R.8Hearts.After1": "I've never told anyone about my interest in aviation or my model planes before...#$b#It's nice having someone to share it with, finally.$l",
	"8Hearts.After2": "Have you used that radio at all?#$b#Let me know if you hear anything interesting!$h",

	//10 Heart Event
	//Most of the event is untouched because it's already basically the best one he has. we love balloon in this house
	//Basically all I did was minor personal taste phrasing edits, removing the superfluous fork, and changing the stuff that implies this is like a first date because sir we've been dating for two hearts
	
	"10Hearts.1": "There you are... just in time!",
	"10Hearts.2": "Look, here it comes!$8",
	"10Hearts.3": "Marcello's Balloon Rentals at your service!",
	"10Hearts.4": "Marcello: It's all yours for two hours.",
	"10Hearts.5": "Marcello: Now... I was told there's a saloon somewhere around here?",
	"10Hearts.6": "I saw an ad in the paper for these balloon rides and I knew I had to surprise you with one.",
	"10Hearts.7": "#This looks fun! Let's go!#...But aren't you afraid of heights?",
	"10Hearts.8": "Okay... you first.$l",
	"10Hearts.9": "Yes... I am.$s#$b#But I don't want to let being scared stop me from doing what I want, and experiencing this with you.$l#$b#I'm determined to try.",
	"10Hearts.10": "We... We're up so high...$8",
	"10Hearts.11": "I wanted to impress you with this... but look at me. I'm a trembling coward.$7",
	"10Hearts.12": "#You don't need to try to impress me.#Just open your eyes. It's worth it.#Honestly? I'm also a little afraid of heights.",
	"10Hearts.13": "I just don't want you to get bored of me. You're so much more adventurous than I am...$7",
	"10Hearts.14": "... You're right. I don't want to let myself miss this.",
	"10Hearts.15": "Really?#$b#... And you're up here anyway.$l",
	"10Hearts.16": "That's part of why I like you, @... you have enough courage for the both of us.$l",
	"10Hearts.17": "I'm going to open my eyes and look down... don't let go of my hand.",
	"10Hearts.18": "Okay. Okay, I think I can do it now.$8",
	"10Hearts.19": "Hey, this is incredible! I think I can see Mayor Lewis standing in the town square!$h",
	"10Hearts.20": "Ha... if you'd told me last year that I'd be doing this now, I wouldn't have believed you.",
	"10Hearts.21": "Um... @? I just wanted to say that I... uh...$7",
	//local man probably had a whole speech planned and completely forgot it the second he went to say it. rip in piss babe
	"10Hearts.22": "...$l",
	"10Hearts.23": "Whoops... Our time was up half an hour ago. We'd better touch down.$l",
	"10Hearts.After": "I haven't had such a wonderful day in as long as I can remember.$l",

	//12 Heart Event

	//A fun thing I learned: if your house doesn't have a fireplace in it, your dinner table with Harvey will spawn in THE VOID.
	//So uh.... have a fireplace. Or don't. I'm not your dad.

	"12Hearts.1": "Hmm... Needs salt...",
	"12Hearts.2": "It's burning!",
	"12Hearts.3": "Phew... Haha. Okay.",
	"12Hearts.4": "If that's the worst that happens...",
	"12Hearts.5": "Then tonight will be great!",
	"12Hearts.6": "Presto!",
	"12Hearts.7": "Ah... You're right on time, @!$h#$b#Let me just set the table...",
	"12Hearts.8": "You've been working so hard on the farm... I thought it might be nice to surprise you with a romantic dinner.",
	"12Hearts.9": "It's my very own 'angel hair pasta primavera'...#$b#I decided to take bit of a risk and not follow a recipe.$h#$b#I hope you like it.$l",
	"12Hearts.10": "#It tastes just heavenly#It tastes fresh and healthy#It tastes a little smoky",
	"12Hearts.11": "Heavenly, huh? That must be the 'angel hair'!$h",
	"12Hearts.12": "Oh yes, I forgot to mention... it's whole wheat pasta, and I used plenty of farm-fresh vegetables.#$b#So in a way you helped make it too!$h",
	"12Hearts.13": "Oh... ha. There was a bit in the middle there where things got dicey.#$b$I tried to give myself most of the burnt bits.",
	"12Hearts.14": "Anyway, I think it came out relatively well, for an experiment.",
	"12Hearts.15": "What about you? Did you do anything interesting today?",
	"12Hearts.16": "#I did chores around the farm#I went spelunking in the caves#I focused on fishing#I caught up with friends#I was all over the place#I can't remember#Not really, no",
	"12Hearts.17": "Yes, I can still see the dirt in your hair!#$b#Oh, it doesn't bother me. It's part of your charm.$h",
	"12Hearts.18": "The, uh... the ones full of monsters?$7#$b#... Well, I'm glad you came home in one piece. It amazes me how much you're capable of.",
	"12Hearts.19": "A day out by the water, huh? Sounds relaxing...#$b#Unless the fish were being difficult!$h",
	"12Hearts.20": "Oh, good! That sounds like a great way to spend the day.#$b#How is everyone in town?",
	"12Hearts.21": "That makes sense. There's lots to do in this valley and only so many hours in the day!#$b#Hopefully this was a nice break after all that running around.$h",
	"12Hearts.22": "Ah... I have that problem sometimes, too.$s#$b#That might be a sign you're working yourself too hard. Remember to rest sometimes, alright?",
	"12Hearts.23": "Took the day off, huh?#$b#Good. Not every day needs to be interesting. Little moments like this are nice, too.$l",
	"12Hearts.24": "You and Harvey enjoy a nice conversation with your meal...",
	"12Hearts.25": "... and before you know it you've been talking for hours.",
	"12Hearts.26": "#Wow, how did it get so late?#$b#I should probably think about going to bed or I'll be falling asleep at my desk tomorrow.|Wow, it got late, didn't it?#$b#At least I don't have to work tomorrow.$h",
	"12Hearts.27": "Don't worry about the dishes. I'll take care of those.",
	"12Hearts.28": "Oh, think of it this way: I almost set the kitchen on fire, cleaning it up should be my job.#$b#Besides, I like doing things for you. I cook and keep the house tidy so that when you come home you don't have to worry about it.#$b#It's one of the little ways I try to show you that I love you.$l",
	"12Hearts.29": "Tonight really was wonderful. We should do this again soon, @.$h",
	"12Hearts.after": "I know it's not nearly as exciting as the things you do every day, but not using a recipe is something I never would have done before I met you.#$e#You really are the best thing that's ever happened to me.$l",
	
	//Mail
	
	"IntroMail": "Hello, Farmer @.^^Please stop by the clinic when you have a moment. I would like to discuss your medical care now that you're a part of our community.^^Welcome again, by the way!^^ - Dr. Harvey",
	"IntroMailName": "Invitation to the Clinic",
	"8HeartsMail": "@,^^I'm sorry that I was so frazzled yesterday. I don't get many visitors, so when you stopped by it was a surprise.^^Not a bad one! Just unexpected.^^Anyway... I was reorganizing my desk and found this. I thought you might like to have it. If you ever want to listen to the planes go by, you can tune it to frequency 140.^^- Harvey",
	"8HeartsMailName": "A Gift From Harvey",
	
	//Weekly Dialogue
	//Because of how the randomization is set up, $query, $q, %revealtaste and other commands need to be in these strings directly. 
	//IF YOU USE AN AI OR A PROGRAM TO TRANSLATE AND IT MESSES THOSE UP, YOU'RE ON YOUR OWN, BUCKAROO!

	"Mon.1": "We sell a few over-the-counter medications at the clinic... feel free to stop by if you're feeling exhausted.",
	"Mon.2": "I know that being a farmer is pretty tiring work... don't overdo it!",
	"Mon.3": "What are your plans for this coming week, @?#$e#Nothing too dangerous, I hope.",
	"Mon.4": "I feel responsible for the health of this whole community... it's kind of stressful.#$e#It's a small town, and I'm fortunate to be able to build a good relationship with my patients.#$b#But that comes with its own problems...$s",
	"Mon.5": "There's only so much we can realistically handle at the clinic.#$e#Part of being a good doctor is knowing when to refer your patient to someone else.",
	"Mon.6": "Sometimes I feel as though I wake up tired. Do you ever have days like that?",
	"Mon.7": "I have an entire drawer in my kitchen full of recipes I've clipped out of magazines.#$b#In theory it's a great idea but in practice I don't think I open the drawer unless I'm putting another one in.$h",
	"Mon.8": "I think I'd like to stay in Stardew Valley permanently. I'm finally starting to feel involved in the community.#$e#It feels good to know that you're liked as well as useful.",
	"Mon.9": "I've started really making an effort to cook more regularly.#$e#You're welcome to come over for dinner sometime, @. Having someone else to cook for would be nice.$h",
	"Mon.10": "Lately I've been feeling like a weight's been lifted off my shoulders.#$b#It's funny; I got so used to it that I almost didn't notice it was there until it was gone.",
	
	"Tue.1": "It's a beautiful day, isn't it?#$e#I wish I had less work to do.$s",
	"Tue.2": "If you ever have questions and I'm not available, ask Maru.#$b#She's very knowledgeable.$h",
	"Tue.3": "There's a documentary about the medical practices of ancient civilizations on TV later tonight.#$b#Hopefully I'll finish my reports in time for it.$s",
	"Tue.4": "I have to do a lot of reading to keep up with the best practices for patient care.#$e#At least I like reading!$h",
	"Tue.5": "I want to form a good rapport with my patients, but getting too close presents a conflict of interest.$s#$b#It's a difficult balance to maintain.#$e#We can be friendly, but we can't entirely be friends.",
	"Tue.6": "Did you know you can develop allergies later in life?#$b#It happens very commonly with shellfish, actually.",
	"Tue.7": "It's difficult knowing that no matter how much advice I give, it's up to my patients whether or not they take it.#$e#There are some people in this town I worry about quite a lot.$s",
	"Tue.8": "Don't overwork yourself, @. #$e#If our farmers get sick, where will we get our food? We need you!$h",
		"R.Tue.8": "Don't overwork yourself, @.#$e#Your health is important to me.",
	"Tue.9": "It's good to see you, @.$h#$e#I admit it's nice to have something to get out of bed for besides work.$l",
	"Tue.10": "They say that just smiling more can improve your health.#$e#I was always a little dubious about that.#$b#Being with you is starting to convince me, though.$h",

	"Wed.1": "Remember to cover your mouth when you sneeze.#$e#Then make sure to wash your hands.",
	"Wed.2": "It's a great help having Maru working at the clinic.#$e#She invented an entirely new way of organizing our records. It's much more intuitive!$h",
	"Wed.3": "I moved here right after graduating my residency.#$e#That would have been... wow. Longer ago than I thought.$s",
	"Wed.4": "I swear I do leave the clinic sometimes.#$b#I'm often at the museum on Saturdays, if you're ever on that side of town.$h",
	"Wed.5": "I've found that it's good for my health to try and stay positive.#$e#It's not always easy, but I do think you can find a silver lining on any cloud if you look hard enough.",
	"Wed.6": "It's nice to have another friend in town.$h#$e# I always worried that I was boring Maru when it was just the two of us.",
	"Wed.7": "You know, I had a lot of acquaintances during my time in medical school...#$b#I don't know if I ever had any actual friends.$s",
	"Wed.8": "It's funny. In an emergency situation I almost forget to be afraid: all that matters is taking care of the patient.#$e$It usually only catches up to me afterwards.$s#$b#That's probably better than the alternative.",
	"Wed.9": "You have a really healthy glow. That's good.$h",
	"Wed.10": "Usually by the middle of the week I'd be starting to hit a slump.#$b#I think your energy is infectious!$h",
	
	"Thu.1": "I live above the clinic. I admit it's convenient, not having a commute.",
	"Thu.2": "Nutrition is important, so make sure and eat well. #$b#$q TH2Pos/TH2Neg TH2None#Home-cooked meals are best. Do you cook?#$r TH2Pos 25 TH2Yes#I love to cook!#$r TH2Pos 0 TH2Busy#I'm usually too busy...#$r TH2Neg -5 TH2No#I have more important things to spend time on.",
	"TH2Yes": "That's good! You'll have no trouble staying healthy, then.$h",
	"TH2Busy": "Ah, yes. I know how that is.$s#$b#Still, even the occasional healthy meal is better than none.",
	"TH2No":  "Ah... right. I'm sure you're very busy with the farm.$s",
	"TH2None": "$p TH2Neg#Maybe take advantage of all that fresh produce.|... Sorry. I should take my doctor's hat off, sometimes.$h",
	"Thu.3": "I'm what you'd call a family practice physician.#$e#Taking care of someone from birth to death... that's a lot of responsibility. I take it very seriously.",
	"Thu.4": "I probably drink more coffee than is strictly healthy.$s#$e#But all that paperwork wouldn't get done otherwise!",
	"Thu.5": "I try and attend every town festival, even if I find crowds overwhelming.#$e#It's good for me to get out of the clinic sometimes.",
	"Thu.6": "%revealtaste:Maru:432 I tried making my own pickles once.#$b#I think I'm the reason Maru won't eat them now.$s",
	"Thu.7": "Do you ever listen to music while you're working?#$b#I find it helps the time go by much more quickly.$h",
	"Thu.8": "I always wanted to work in a smaller, underserved community.#$b#It can vastly improve quality of life to have easier access to medical care.#$e#Imagine how much crankier George would be if he had to go all the way to Zuzu City for his checkups!$h",
	"Thu.9": "I wrote the wrong date on a report the other day.#$e#I was thinking about you and got distracted.$l",
	"Thu.10": "Maintaining work-life balance has always been something I struggle with.$s#$e#If I didn't live alone I think it would be easier.$l",

	"Fri.1": "Feel free to stop by my office if you're ever feeling ill.#$e#Though the farming lifestyle is very active. You'll probably stay healthy without trying.$h",
	"Fri.2": "Remember to stay hydrated. You'd be surprised at how many people don't drink enough water.",
	"Fri.3": "Any exciting plans for the weekend, @?#$e#Remember, everything in moderation!",
	"Fri.4": "You're welcome to visit me at my apartment any time you like.#$e#I don't often have company. It would be a nice change of pace.",
	"Fri.5": "I've found that being a doctor is very fulfilling work.#$e#I've always felt happiest when I'm helping other people.",
	"Fri.6": "It's kind of you to make time to talk with me, @.#$b#It always brightens my day.$h",
	"Fri.7": "Living where I work makes some things easier... on the other hand, it makes it difficult to ever stop working.",
	"Fri.8": "I had a phase as a child where I was convinced I wanted to be a jazz pianist.#$b#At my first recital I threw up before I even got on stage. I never played the piano again.#$e#It was mortifying then but it's kind of funny now.$h",
	"Fri.9": "I've been thinking about setting up a little herb garden in my window.#$e#If you have any tips for keeping plants alive, I'd love to hear them.$h",
	"Fri.10": "@, I know I'm not technically your doctor...#$b#But if you ever need a 'confidential checkup' you know where to find me.$l",

	"Sat.1": "I never really relax, even on weekends.#$e#It's not as though I can say 'sorry, it's my day off' if there's a medical emergency.",
	"Sat.2": "Did you know the museum library has an extensive microfiche collection?#$e# It's fascinating to read news articles from decades ago. Things were very different then.",
	"Sat.3": "I imagine even on weekends the farm requires a lot of attention.#$e#Ha... you and I both have jobs that it's hard to ever really put down.",
	"Sat.4": "Are you sleeping enough,@?#$e#At the very least you should be going to bed before midnight.",
	"Sat.5": "I like that Pelican town is small enough that you can walk everywhere.#$e#Driving always made me a little nervous.",
	"Sat.6": "Another week is almost over... it feels like the older I get, the faster they fly by.$s",
	"Sat.7": "I came here because I liked the small-town atmosphere and the potential for a truly holistic approach to patient care.#$e#I've grown to really love it.$h",
	"Sat.8": "Maybe I'll actually take it easy this weekend.#$e#I could finally open that bottle of wine I've been saving.",
	"Sat.9": "%Harvey is humming an upbeat jazz tune and seems completely distracted.",
	"Sat.10": "*Sigh*... I'm starting to feel kind of old...#$e#The older you get the more memories you're burdened with. It can be overwhelming.$s#$e#I think I'll stay younger with you around.$h",

	"Sun.1": "It's always difficult to fully enjoy Sundays, knowing that Monday is just around the corner.",
	"Sun.2": "Hmm... I'm struggling to make ends meet. I don't have enough patients.#$e#I suppose that's the trade-off for working in a rural community.",
	"Sun.3": "Be careful if you're going to go down into the mines.#$e#Remember to wear closed-toed shoes!",
	"Sun.4": "As a doctor, I'm well aware of the benefits of home-cooked food. But I'm so busy, I have a hard time bringing myself to cook.",
	"Sun.5": "I'd strongly recommend against drinking Joja Cola.#$e#I've read the ingredient list and it's... concerning.$s",
	"Sun.6": "My colleagues in Zuzu City keep telling me I should move there if money's so tight out here.#$e#I tried city life during medical school and I can say with confidence that it's not for me. Far too fast-paced.",
	"Sun.7": "Medical school was difficult, but I've never regretted the decision to pursue it.#$b#It's more than a career for me; it's a vocation. It gives me purpose.",
	"Sun.8": "Imagine having a patient's life completely in your hands, and failing to keep them alive... that's something that will haunt you forever.$s#$e#Hypothetically.",
	"Sun.9": "Some people know what they want to do with their lives from a very young age. I envy that.#$e#It took me a lot of false starts to get to where I am and I've always felt a little behind because of it.",
	"Sun.10": "Do you ever get lonely living by yourself on the farm, @?#$e#Just wondering.$l",

	"Spring.Weekly.0.1": "It's officially pollen season.#$b#Living in the countryside seems like it would be a little less idyllic for a person with bad allergies.",
	"Spring.Weekly.0.2": "%revealtaste:Harvey:22 Did you know that dandelion greens are edible?#$b#Most people consider them weeds, but they're not bad in a salad.",
	"Spring.Weekly.0.3": "If there's something that you need from the clinic, I'd advise stopping by earlier in the day.",
	"Spring.Weekly.0.4": "Be sure to cook any fish you catch thoroughly before you eat it.",

	"Spring.Weekly.2.1": "Hi, @. Are you having a productive Spring so far?#$e#Remember not to give yourself more work than you can comfortably handle.",
	"Spring.Weekly.2.2": "It's Spring cleaning season again. It must take a lot of work to keep %farm Farm tidy.",
	"Spring.Weekly.2.3": "Remember to eat a healthy breakfast before you start in on your farm chores.#$e#It's the most important meal of the day, as they say.",
	"Spring.Weekly.2.4": "Maru works at the clinic on Tuesdays and Thursdays.#$e#She's been a huge help since she started.",

	"Spring.Weekly.4.1": "%revealtaste:Harvey:18 My favorite flower is the daffodil.#$e#They're not particularly exciting, but they're bright and cheerful, and they come back reliably every year.$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.4.2": "%revealtaste:Harvey:399 Patches of spring onions grow down past Marnie's barn, across the river.#$e#I'd go pick some myself if my schedule wasn't so tight.",
	"Spring.Weekly.4.3": "I really need to put aside time to clear out the magazines in the clinic waiting room...#$e#There are definitely some in there old enough to qualify as historical documents.",
	"Spring.Weekly.4.4": "Spring means the days are getting longer again.#$e#And yet I still feel like I never have enough time to get everything done.",

	"Spring.Weekly.6.1": "Sometimes I feel as though I put so much energy into taking care of my patients that I don't have any left over to take care of myself...$s#$e#...Ah! I'm fine though, really!$8",
	"Spring.Weekly.6.2": "%revealtaste:Maru:400 Spring is strawberry season.#$b#It's all Maru talks about this time of year. They're her favorite.",
	"Spring.Weekly.6.3": "I've thought about getting a pet to keep me company.#$e#My apartment barely has enough room in it for me, though, let alone a cat or a dog.#$b#I'd feel bad keeping one cooped up in there.$s",
	"Spring.Weekly.6.4": "I've been reading a book about historical agricultural practices. It's just fascinating!$h#$b#You're welcome to borrow it when I'm done, if you want.",

	"Spring.Weekly.8.1": "There's a bird's nest in the tree outside my clinic. If you look closely you can see the eggs!$h#$b#Not too closely, though, or mama bird will get mad.",
	"Spring.Weekly.8.2": "Would you like to join me on my afternoon walks sometimes, @?#$e#Walking is an easy way to stay active, but it's more fun with company!$h",
		"R.Spring.Weekly.8.2": "Would you like to join me on my afternoon walks sometimes, @?#$e#I'd like it if you did.$l",
	"Spring.Weekly.8.3": "Have you planted any flowers this Spring, @?#$e#I wish I had the space for a flower garden.#$b#I'm a little jealous of you!$h",
		"R.Spring.Weekly.8.3": "Oh, @, this is for you. I thought you might like it. [591 597 18]$l",
	"Spring.Weekly.8.4": "I never have to worry about setting my alarm clock in Spring.#$b#The birds outside my window are always loud enough to wake me up before it goes off.$h",

	"Spring.Weekly.10.1": "The flowers look brighter this year, somehow.#$e#Or maybe I'm just noticing them more.$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.10.2": "There's always an upswing in air-traffic this time of year.#$e#It's not surprising that people enjoy flying more when it's nice out.",
	"Spring.Weekly.10.3": "It's been so pleasant outside since the season turned... we should plan a picnic!$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.10.4": "Spending time with you always puts a Spring in my step.$l#$e#Haha. Too much?$h", 

	"Summer.Weekly.0.1": "Be careful running around in the tall grass! Watch out for bees.",
	"Summer.Weekly.0.2": "It feels like a shame that I spend so much of Summer indoors...$s#$e#Oh, well. It can't be helped.",
	"Summer.Weekly.0.3": "If you're planning to stay out in the sun for extended periods of time, I'd recommend a hat.",
	"Summer.Weekly.0.4": "When applying sunscreen, don't forget to put some behind your ears.",

	"Summer.Weekly.2.1": "Sometimes there's broken glass in the sand at the beach.#$e#Be careful where you step if you walk around near the water without shoes on.",
	"Summer.Weekly.2.2": "Remember to drink plenty of water and give yourself regular breaks.#$e#I know you have a lot to do on the farm, but heat stroke is no joke!",
	"Summer.Weekly.2.3": "If you're looking for something to do with your time, it's always worth it to check the bulletin board outside of Pierre's shop.",
	"Summer.Weekly.2.4": "If you often find yourself a target for mosquitos, you're more likely to have Type O blood.#$e#At least, anecdotal evidence suggests that's the flavor they like best.",

	"Summer.Weekly.4.1": "You can see a lot of unique wildlife down at the tidepools by the beach.#$e#Be careful of the urchins! Some of them are venomous, and none of them like to be stepped on.",
	"Summer.Weekly.4.2": "It probably seems silly to drink hot coffee when the weather is like this.#$e#I'm a creature of habit, I suppose.",
	"Summer.Weekly.4.3": "If you have a moment, can you help me with something?#$b#Oh, it's nothing serious, don't worry!$h#$b#$q SW43Pollywogs/SW43Tadpoles SW43None#Do you call baby frogs 'pollywogs' or 'tadpoles'? #$r SW43Pollywogs 10 SW43P#Pollywogs, obviously. #$r SW43Tadpoles 0 SW43T#Tadpoles, obviously.",
	"SW43P": "Me too! I know it's not terribly scientific, but I still prefer it.$h#$e#Maru thinks it must be a 'regional' thing.",
	"SW43T": "Ah... that's what Maru said too.#$e#Am I the only one who says 'pollywogs'?",
	"SW43None": "$p SW43Pollywogs #Just tell Maru you say 'pollywogs' too. She won't believe me.#$e#Between you and me, I think she's being contrary on purpose.|A lizard got into the clinic somehow and I'm not exactly fast enough to catch it.",
	"Summer.Weekly.4.4": "It might seem counter-intuitive, but you should actually up your salt intake when it's hot out.#$e#Salt helps your body hang on to all that water you should be drinking.",

	"Summer.Weekly.6.1": "You know, I've never taken a Summer vacation.#$b#It's always difficult to justify setting aside the time...",
	"Summer.Weekly.6.2": "Caroline told me once that I'd be less nervous if I replaced my morning coffee with tea.#$e#I don't know if it would really make much of a difference.",
	"Summer.Weekly.6.3": "Summer is definitely my least favorite season.#$e#There's nothing objectively wrong with it, but it's a reminder that the year is half-gone already.",
	"Summer.Weekly.6.4": "Have you seen any butterflies while out and about?#$b#They're very common this time of year.",

	"Summer.Weekly.8.1": "I don't get a lot of free time, so I never know how to spend it when I have some.#$b#It's kind of a silly problem to have.$h",
	"Summer.Weekly.8.2": "I've recently taken an interest in birding.#$e#We often get visited by parrots from the Fern Islands here.$h",
		"R.Summer.Weekly.8.2": "Are you looking forward to seeing the Moonlight Jellies this year?#$b#I'm excited to watch them with you.$l",
	"Summer.Weekly.8.3": "You're lucky you can spend so much time outside and never get a sunburn.#$e#I feel like I start turning red the second I leave the clinic.",
		"R.Summer.Weekly.8.3": "Do you ever get freckles from spending so long outside in the sun?#$e#You'd look cute with freckles.$l",
	"Summer.Weekly.8.4": "Have you ever heard owls out by your farm at night?#$e#The whole time I've been living here, I've never managed to spot one.",

	"Summer.Weekly.10.1": "It's so nice out that I've been considering playing hooky from work.$#e#@, I think you might be a bad influence!#h",
	"Summer.Weekly.10.2": "I got a call from one of my old colleagues the other day. ${He's^She's^They're}$ getting married.#$e#It feels like everyone my age is starting to settle down.",
	"Summer.Weekly.10.3": "Here, @. I thought you might like this. Remember to put it in water so it doesn't wilt in the heat. [421 376 593]$l",
	"Summer.Weekly.10.4": "It's been so difficult to focus on my work lately.#$b#You know, because of the heat.$l",

	"Fall.Weekly.0.1": "This is a particularly good season for foraging.#$e#This might be obvious, but make sure to check that what you find is edible before you eat it.",
	"Fall.Weekly.0.2": "Vinegar is useful in cooking, but it also makes a good natural cleaner.#$b#That is, if you don't mind your kitchen smelling like vinegar.",
	"Fall.Weekly.0.3": "If you start to feel under the weather, don't try to just 'push through'.#$e#It will take you twice as long to get better.",
	"Fall.Weekly.0.4": "Have you started preparing %farm Farm for winter?#$e#Remember to stock up on firewood.",

	"Fall.Weekly.2.1": "In addition to being festive, pumpkins are actually an excellent source of fiber and Vitamin A.",
	"Fall.Weekly.2.2": "PLACEHOLDER 2.2",
	"Fall.Weekly.2.3": "The days will start getting shorter soon. Make sure to plan your farm chores accordingly so you don't get overwhelmed.",
	"Fall.Weekly.2.4": "PLACEHOLDER 2.4",

	"Fall.Weekly.4.1": "It's true that, financially, fall is the best season for the clinic...#$b#Not that I want anyone to get sick!$8",
	"Fall.Weekly.4.2": "Did you know that you can make oil out of sunflower seeds?#$e#I prefer truffle oil for cooking when I can get it, personally.",
	"Fall.Weekly.4.3": "I take patient confidentiality very seriously.#$b#I think that's especially important in a small town, where gossip can spread quickly.",
	"Fall.Weekly.4.4": "If I had to pick a favorite season, I'd probably say Fall.#$e#It's not too hot, not too cold, and there's always an abundance of mushrooms.$h",

	"Fall.Weekly.6.1": "$query MUSEUM_DONATIONS 10 Arch #From what I understand, Stardew Valley is actually an archeological hotspot.#$e#But you'd know all about that, judging by the donations in the museum.$h|From what I understand, Stardew Valley is actually an archeological hotspot.#$e#It makes sense that Gunther decided to settle here.",
	"Fall.Weekly.6.2": "I keep thinking I ought to set up a bird feeder.#$e#I wonder if Robin would be interested in building me one...?",
	"Fall.Weekly.6.3": "I've seen several flocks of birds heading South.#$e#Is it weird to feel a little jealous of them?",
	"Fall.Weekly.6.4": "I imagine decorating for the season is easy for you.#$b#You probably already have a scarecrow up, right?$h",

	"Fall.Weekly.8.1": "When I was younger I used to stay up late reading by the light of my nightlight.#$e#I think that might be part of the reason my eyesight is so bad now...",
	"Fall.Weekly.8.2": "My apartment here is small, but it's still quite a bit larger than the one I had as a student.#$e#When I first moved in it felt downright spacious.",
		"R.Fall.Weekly.8.2": "@, I just finished a book I think you'd enjoy. Here, check it out and tell me what you think. [(F)PurpleBook (F)BlueBook (F)YellowBook (F)Redbook (F)GreenBook (F)BrownBook PurpleBook]",
	"Fall.Weekly.8.3": "I've never really liked Spirit's Eve, but I do like the excuse to roast a bunch of pumpkin seeds.$h",
		"R.Fall.Weekly.8.3": "Normally I try to stay away from candy, even around Spirit's Eve season.#$b#Here, you take this off my hands so I'm not tempted. [243 279]$h",
	"Fall.Weekly.8.4": "I've been reading about the historical background of Spirit's Eve.#$e#Did you know that it used to be more about welcoming the end-of-Summer harvest?#$b#It's kind of like a celebration of farmers, that way!$h",

	"Fall.Weekly.10.1": "If you're feeling chilly, @, you're welcome to borrow my coat.$l",
	"Fall.Weekly.10.2": "Here, @. It's a 'hot drinks' kind of day, I think. Stay warm! [395 614]$h",
	"Fall.Weekly.10.3": "You know what I haven't had in years? A genuine home-made apple cider.#$e#I bet between the two of us we could whip up a blue-ribbon batch.$h",
	"Fall.Weekly.10.4": "PLACEHOLDER 10.4",

	//It's so unlikely anyone will still be at 0/1 hearts with him by Winter but I simply have to be thorough lol
	//Also idk some people don't care about him that much and they might also download this mod for ????reasons????
	//idk them idk their life

	"Winter.Weekly.0.1": "I hope that your farmhouse is properly insulated. It gets very cold here in the valley at night.",
	"Winter.Weekly.0.2": "If you find yourself with a cough, honey works just as well as cough syrup.#$e#Just because I'm a doctor doesn't mean I think home remedies are bunk. If it works, it works!$h",
	"Winter.Weekly.0.3": "If you haven't already invested in heavy-duty boots, now would be the time.",
	"Winter.Weekly.0.4": "PLACEHOLDER 0.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.2.1": "I know that holly berries look tempting, but it's definitely a bad idea to eat them.",
	"Winter.Weekly.2.2": "The valley usually spends all winter covered in snow.#$e#I imagine that might make farming more difficult.",
	"Winter.Weekly.2.3": "PLACEHOLDER 2.3",
	"Winter.Weekly.2.4": "PLACEHOLDER 2.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.4.1": "%revealtaste:Harvey:829 You know, you can actually make a nice tea just by boiling fresh ginger.#$e#You can add cinnamon as well if you'd like a more wintery taste.",
	"Winter.Weekly.4.2": "PLACEHOLDER 4.2",
	"Winter.Weekly.4.3": "PLACEHOLDER 4.3",
	"Winter.Weekly.4.4": "PLACEHOLDER 4.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.6.1": "I once asked Elliot for book recommendations...#$e#I think he and I have slightly different tastes when it comes to literature.",
	"Winter.Weekly.6.2": "$query MUSEUM_DONATIONS 40 Arch Minerals #The museum has really filled up thanks to you.#$e#I guess it makes sense, considering how much digging a farmer must do.$h|It always feels special when there's a new donation to the museum, considering how long it was empty.",
	"Winter.Weekly.6.3": "I worry about Linus in this weather.#$b#I know he can take care of himself, of course. But I still worry.#$e#I hope he'd feel comfortable reaching out if he needed help.",
	"Winter.Weekly.6.4": "I will say, a huge upside to living where I work is that I don't have to walk to work in the snow.",

	"Winter.Weekly.8.1": "PLACEHOLDER 8.1",
	"Winter.Weekly.8.2": "PLACEHOLDER 8.2",
		"R.Winter.Weekly.8.2": "@, I just finished a book I think you'd enjoy. Here, check it out and tell me what you think. [(F)PurpleBook (F)BlueBook (F)YellowBook (F)Redbook (F)GreenBook (F)BrownBook PurpleBook]",
	"Winter.Weekly.8.3": "Gift-giving season is always a little stressful for me.#$e#I worry about getting someone something that they don't want, or that they already have.",
		"R.Winter.Weekly.8.3": "Don't stress about getting me the 'perfect' gift this year.#$b#I think I would like most anything that you gave me.$h",
	"Winter.Weekly.8.4": "PLACEHOLDER 8.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.10.1": "Winter always makes me feel a little melancholy...#$b#Less so, this year.$l",
	"Winter.Weekly.10.2": "Here, @. It's a 'hot drinks' kind of day, I think. Stay warm! [395 614]$h",
	"Winter.Weekly.10.3": "This time of year always makes me wish I had a fireplace.#$e#The one in your cabin must be so cozy.$l",
	"Winter.Weekly.10.4": "PLACEHOLDER 10.4",
	
	//Date Specific Dialogue
	
	"Fall.Plans":"I enjoy taking walks the most in fall; the air is brisk and the leaves are at their most visually stunning.",
		"R.Fall.Plans": "Did you have plans for this weekend?#$b#I was thinking maybe we could get coffee.",
	"Spring.FlowerDance": "The Flower Dance is tomorrow...#$b#I'm not really much of a dancer, but Maru always insists that if she has to go, I have to go.",
		"R.Spring.FlowerDance": "Will I see you at the Flower Dance tomorrow?$l",
	"Fall.Mushrooms": "Did you know many of the mushrooms that grow locally are edible?$#b#Be careful of the red ones, though.",
	"Fall.Chilly": "The weather has started to turn.#$b#Add more layers if you start feeling chilly.",
	"Winter.FluShots": "Don't forget to get your flu shot this year.#$e#An ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure, as they say.",
	"Winter.AlmostBirthday.": "%Harvey appears to be quieter than usual. You should probably leave him be.",
		"R.Winter.AlmostBirthday.": "Well... tomorrow's my birthday. Every year it gets harder to get excited about it.",
	"Winter.End": "Winter has its charm, but I'm looking forward to seeing the sun more often in Spring.",
	
	//Festival Dialogue
	//some of these haven't been edited yet but are here in the i18n in preparation for when I think of a better line OR when/if I commit to randomized dialogue options here too
	
	"fall16.1": "It's easy to forget how large pigs are until you're looking at them in person...",
	"fall16.2": "Robin and Leah both have very impressive woodworking skills.#$b#Though I do worry that they aren't wearing gloves...",
	"fall16.1.spouse": "Let me know when you're ready to go home, @. I'll just be over here.",
	"fall16.2.spouse": "Good luck today in the competition, @. I have full confidence in you!$h",
	
	"fall27.1": "I think this is about as far as I'm going to get this year.$s",
	"fall27.2": "Oh! @!$8#$b#I was just... uh...#$b#...The truth is, I got scared and got all turned around and now I can't find my way out. Don't tell anyone.$s",
	"fall27.1.spouse": "Hi... I was hoping I would run into you in here...$l",
	"fall27.2.spouse": "On your way through the maze, @? Good luck!$h#$e#Oh, I'll be fine. You go ahead.$0",

	"spring13.1": "The eggs in the egg hunt were colored with food-grade dyes, so you can technically eat them.#$b#I wouldn't, though. They've been out of the fridge a little too long for comfort.$s",
	"spring13.2": "Eggs are fine, but I'd advise against eating thirty per day!",
	"spring13.1.spouse": "Are you going to participate in the egg hunt?#$b#I'm sure you'll give Abigail a run for her money!$h",

	"spring24.1": "Maru and I usually come to this event as friends.#$b#It's like highschool prom all over again.$s",
	"spring24.2": "I've been thinking lately that a lot of things in life are about perspective.#$b#There are worse things than an ill-fitting suit and a few minutes of awkward dancing.$h",
		"R.spring24": "#Oh, @... you look ${great^lovely^wonderful}$.$l",
	"FlowerDanceSpouse.1": "I've been looking forward to it all afternoon.$l",
	"FlowerDanceSpouse.2": "Of course! I was hoping you would ask.$l#$b#Not that I was ever really worried you wouldn't.$h",
	"FlowerDanceSpouse.3": "I would love to. I don't even find it all that embarassing anymore!$h",
	"FlowerDanceAccept": "You want to dance... with me?#$b#I mean!$8#$b#Yes. Yes, I would like that.$h",
	"FlowerDanceDecline": "Oh! Ah, no thank you.#$b#It's embarrassing enough without making a fool of myself in front of someone I barely know.$s",

	"summer11.1": "Good thing I came with sunscreen.#$e#I feel as though I'm the only one who ever remembers to bring it.",
	"summer11.1.spouse": "Here, @. Let me put some more sunscreen on your shoulders. I don't want you getting burned!",
	"summer11.2": "*pant*... *pant*... ahhhh, I can't wait for a bowl of piping hot soup...$h",
	"summer11.2.spouse": "Hot soup has never made sense to me as the centerpiece for a Summer festival.#$e#One of these years we should try a gazpacho.",

	"summer28.1": "Well, summer's over. To be honest, I'll be happy to say goodbye to these blasted mosquitos!",
	"summer28.2": "It'll be any moment now when the jellies show up... It never gets old!",
	"summer28.2.spouse": "You know... this feels even more magical now that I get to share it with you.$l",

	"winter8.1": "Extreme temperatures can put your body under a lot of stress, so make sure to bundle up!#$e#Oh, and enjoy the festival!$h",
	"winter8.2": "I shouldn't have waxed my moustache this morning, it's frozen solid! Oh dear...$2#$e#Well, if you need an ice pick, you know where to find me...$h",
	"winter8.1.spouse": "Not that I'm not having a good time, but I'm definitely looking forward to going home to our warm fire.$l",
	"winter8.2.spouse": "Good luck today in the ice fishing contest. Do you think you'll beat your score from last year?",

	"winter25.1": "This year, I'm thankful for the continued good health of my patients.",
	"winter25.2": "Every year around this time I rewatch \"The Miracle at Colstar Ranch\".#$b#It's become one of my favorite traditions.$h",
	"winter25.1.spouse": "I'm feeling a little overwhelmed... thank goodness for this crisp air...$l",
	"winter25.2.spouse": "You know, this is my favorite festival.#$b#I'm so glad I get to share it with you, now.$l",
	"WinterStar_GiveGift_Before_Spouse": "Surprise!$h#$b#You have no idea how hard it's been keeping this a secret.",
	"WinterStar_GiveGift_Before": "Hi, @. I'm your gift giver this year.",
	"WinterStar_GiveGift_After": "I hope you like it. I tried to think of something you'd find useful.$h",
	"WinterStar_ReceiveGift": "Oh! Thank you, @.#$b#You have a great poker face. I had no idea it was you!$h",
	"R.WinterStar_ReceiveGift": "Oh! Thank you, @.#$b#It must have been difficult keeping this a secret from me. I appreciate the effort.$h",
	
	//Marriage Dialogue
	//Static Marriage Dialogue
	
	"Marriage.spring_1": "The explosion of life at the start of a new year is invigorating, don't you think?#$e#Maybe I'll get my paperwork out of the way early today.",
	"Marriage.spring_8": "The birds that left for the Winter have started coming back.#$e#I'm sure there's a science behind how they navigate. I should look it up.",
	"Marriage.spring_12": "Good luck in the egg hunt tomorrow!$h#$e#Of course I'll be there to watch, even if I'm not a big fan of the crowd...",
	"Marriage.spring_23": "Will you dance with me at the festival tomorrow?$7#$e#It's one of my favorite parts of the year.$l",
	"Marriage.spring_25": "Hm... my 'to read' list is getting pretty short.#$b#Any recommendations?",
	"Marriage.summer_1": "Make sure you don't get sunburnt, @!$8#$b#I've stocked up on sunscreen, so be sure to put some on before you go out.",
	"Marriage.summer_8": "I didn't sleep so well last night... it's difficult to get comfortable in this heat.$s",
	"Marriage.summer_10": "I'm always a little leery of the Luau soup.#$b#It can't be healthy to just toss a bunch of random ingredients into a pot, right?",
	"Marriage.summer_15": "I saw an ant in here earlier, so I put down some diatomaceous earth to keep them out.#$e#I'm not going to share the kitchen with them!$a",
	"Marriage.summer_23": "I spread some fresh diatomaceous earth where the ants were coming in last time.#$b#I saw one this morning and I'm taking no chances.$a",
	"Marriage.summer_27": "The days are going to start getting shorter soon.#$b#Sorry in advance if I seem a little withdrawn... lack of sunlight can have a negative impact on mood.",
	"Marriage.fall_1": "Make sure and diversify your harvests this fall, @.#$e#Or you could just fill every plot with pumpkins.$#b#I'll figure out what to cook with them!$h",
	"Marriage.fall_11": "We have a lot to do to prepare for winter.#$b#You make sure we're stocked up on firewood and I'll get the extra blankets and winter coats out of storage.",
	"Marriage.fall_15": "Tomorrow's the Fair. I'm interested to see what you've been saving for your grange display!$h",
	"Marriage.fall_18": "This is the time of year when the weather really starts to turn... maybe consider a scarf?",
	"Marriage.fall_26": "Out of all the festivals, Spirit's Eve is easily my least favorite.#$b#I know it's all props and makeup, but I just don't find being scared much fun.",
	"Marriage.winter_1": "Be sure to dress warmly in the coming weeks, @.#$b#I know you and I know you'll be out of the house most days even if there's no farming to do!$h",
	"Marriage.winter_7": "It might be nice to attend the festival tomorrow.#$b#Or we could stay in and drink cocoa. I'd be happy with either.#h",
	"Marriage.winter_11": "How are we doing on firewood?#$b#I wouldn't want to run low.",
	"Marriage.winter_13": "Well... I'll be another year older tomorrow. Before I met you that would have bothered me.#$b#Now it almost feels like an accomplishment!$h",
	"Marriage.winter_28": "I can't believe how quickly this year went by.#$b#Well! Here's to many more, huh?$h",
	
	"jobLeave.1": "I have to go into the clinic today. Have a nice day, okay?",
	"jobLeave.2": "I'm going in to work today. Let me know if you need anything from town while I'm there.",
	"jobLeave.3": "Almost time for my morning walk to work! It's such a nice way to get regular exercise.$h",
	"jobLeave.4": "Ah, I won't be able to finish my coffee before I leave for work...$s#$b#I guess I'll just take it with me.",
	"jobLeave.5": "Good morning, @. I'll be at the clinic today if you need me for anything.",
	"jobLeave.6": "I have work to do at the clinic today. I'll see you tonight, @.",
	"jobReturn.1": "Hi, @. Did you have a good day?#$e#My patients are still healthy, so I can't complain.$h",
	"jobReturn.2": "I have to admit, I like going to work a lot more now that I have you to come home to.$l",
	"jobReturn.3": "Oof... I'm exhausted. Being a doctor isn't a physically difficult job, but it's very emotionally demanding.$s",
	"jobReturn.4": "Good evening, @. I just got home a little bit ago. What have you been up to?",
	"jobReturn.5": "The clinic was quiet today. In my line of work I suppose that's a good thing.",
	"jobReturn.6": "What a long day... I think I'm going to relax for the rest of the night.",
	
	"jobVisit.1": "Hi @. What are you doing at the clinic?#$e#Ah, you just came to see me. That's nice.$h",
	"jobVisit.2": "Oh, hello! Sorry, I'm a little busy right now.#$b#Not that it's not always good to see you.$l",
	"jobVisit.3": "%Harvey is counting something under his breath and looks deep in thought. Maybe it's better to leave him be while he's working.",
	"jobVisit.4": "Oh, hello, @. It's good to see you!#$e#It's been a quiet day. That's good, but it does make time go more slowly.#$b#You're always a welcome distraction!$h",
	"jobVisit.5": "It's strange seeing all my old things upstairs still.#$b#I wonder if that space could be converted into something else...",
	"jobVisit.6": "Between you and me, sometimes I take a lollipop out of the jar meant for the kids.#$e#It's fine, they're sugar-free!$h",

	"Marriage.Mon.0.1": "Hi! Did you forget something we needed to put on the grocery list?",
	"Marriage.Mon.0.2": "Hello, @. I'm just picking up some essentials.#$e#And maybe a few fancy spices.#$b#I don't know what I'll do with them yet, but that's part of the fun of it.$h",
	"Marriage.Mon.0.3": "It's nice to come into town and see everyone from time to time.#$e#Somewhere other than the clinic, I mean.",
	"Marriage.Mon.0.4": "Oh, good to see you. Did you come in to drop off some produce for Pierre?",
	"Marriage.Mon.0.5": "Oh, you're here. Good timing; I wanted to ask you your thoughts on fettuccine versus pappardelle.",
	"Marriage.Mon.0.6": "Hm... Pierre's out of the medium roast I like... I guess I could try a light roast?",
	"Marriage.Mon.2.1": "%Harvey is completely absorbed in his book. The title reads: \"Radio Ettiquette: Don't Be a Knob\".",
	"Marriage.Mon.2.2": "%Harvey is reading a book called \"Birds of Ferngill\". There's a very colorful parrot on the cover.",
	"Marriage.Mon.2.3": "%\"Sustainable Farming Under Modern Capitalism\". Huh! Looks like Harvey's taking an interest in your business.",
	"Marriage.Mon.2.4": "$query PLAYER_HAS_CHILDREN current #%The book's title reads \"101 Easy Experiments to Introduce Your Child to Science\". Looks like someone's doing research.|#%The book's title reads \"Historic Wineries of Ferngill\". Looks like someone's doing research.",
	"Marriage.Mon.2.5": "%It looks like Harvey is reading a book called \"A Hip Pocket Guide to Ferngill Mushrooms\".#$b#%On the cover is a man holding a trumpet in one hand and a very large mushroom in the other.",
	"Marriage.Mon.2.6.": "%Harvey's book is titled \"Oh! The Humanity! A History of Aircraft Disasters\". Sounds... fun?",
	
	"spouseRoom.1": "No air-traffic this morning, @. But it's still fun to break out the equipment now and then.",
	"spouseRoom.2": "I'm working on a new model plane. It's so much more relaxing here than in my old apartment.",
	"spouseRoom.3": "I just finished my latest model, @. Would you like to see it?",
	"spouseRoom.4": "It's nice having my own space just for my hobbies. I think it's encouraged me to pursue them more.$h",
	"spouseRoom.5": "Hi, @. Did you need something? Sorry, I was a little distracted.",
	"spouseRoom.6": "If you ever wanted me to show you how to operate my radio, I'd be happy to.",
	
	"OneKid_2": "I want to give %kid1 the best childhood possible.#$b#I think %farm Farm is the perfect place for that.$h",
	"OneKid_3": "So far, I really like being a father!$h#$e#It's not as scary as I thought it would be.",
	"TwoKids_2": "I already gave %kid1 and %kid2 their breakfasts. It's easy to feed them healthy food with so much farm-fresh produce to work with.",
	"TwoKids_3": "%kid1 was playing with one of my planes the other day.#$b#I'm glad I'm not the only one who enjoys them!$h",
	
	//A lot of these didn't NEED editing except they are phrased super weird so I tried to make them less uhhhh Strange
	//I also left out the ones about the NPC spouse being pregnant I'm sorry if you have a trans Harvey mod that I am not aware of
	//If you do oh my god please tell me I'd be all the way into trans Harvey. we can be t4t. T treated him really good to allow for a mustache that nice & im kinda jealous

	"NewChild_SecondChild1": "Our little family has really grown.. it's incredible to think how far we've come together.$l",
	"NewChild_SecondChild2": "Being a father to two beautiful children is like a dream come true. We really have come so far, haven't we?",
	"NewChild_Adoption": "{0} is just perfect... we're so incredibly lucky.",
	"NewChild_FirstChild": "I'm so glad everything went well. You take it easy while we get {0} settled, okay?",
	"NPC.cs.4439": "I wonder if bringing a baby into the house will be too big of a change?$s",
	"NPC.cs.4440": "I hope our adoption request gets approved, {0}. I've got my heart set on being a father.$l",
	"NPC.cs.4441": "Well, {0}, I filed our adoption papers. I double-checked to make sure everything was filled out correctly. Now... we wait.$l",
	"NPC.cs.4447": "I've been reading up on parenting to get ready for when our baby arrives. I'm so excited!$h",
	"NPC.cs.4448": "You have that pregnant glow, {0}. It really suits you.$l",
	
	"Good_0": "I still can barely believe we're married, @. It just doesn't feel real sometimes...$l",
	"Good_1": "I was so lonely before you came into my life... it was awful.$s#$b#Thank you for saving me from that.$l",
	"Good_2": "I think I understand now why they call a spouse your \"other half\".#$b#It's like marrying you filled an empty place in me.$l",
	"Good_3": "Oh, @... you look so ${handsome^beautiful^amazing}$.$l#$e#I mean! Even more than usual.$7",
	"Good_4": "The apartment was just somewhere I lived...#$b#Here, with you? This feels like a real home.$l",
	"Good_5": "I was just admiring my wedding amulet... I never take it off, you know.$l",
	"Good_6": "Be careful, for my sake? I know you're very capable, but I still have nightmares about losing you...$7",
	"Good_7": "I appreciate how hard you work, @.$h#$b#Though... maybe you could take tonight off? We could stay in and open a bottle of wine.$l",
	"Good_8": "I never thought I'd be able to have this kind of life.#$b#I feel so incredibly lucky.$h",
	"Good_9": "You keep my life interesting, @. I don't think I'll ever get bored, living here!$h",
	
	"Neutral_0": "I don't really have anything planned for today.#$e#I guess I could dust the shelves again...",
	"Neutral_1": "How are we doing on groceries?",
	"Neutral_2": "Maybe I'll start a new book. I have a couple I've been meaning to get to.",
	"Neutral_3": "Sorry, @, I can't talk for long. I have a lot of paperwork to get to today.",
	"Neutral_4": "What do you think we should do for dinner tomorrow?",
	"Neutral_5": "@? Is there anything you'd like me to get done today?",
	"Neutral_6": "If you go into town later, could you ask Gunther if he has that book I ordered in from Zuzu Library?",
	"Neutral_7": "I think we might be out of coffee.#$e#I do go through it kind of quickly.$h",
	"Neutral_8": "I've certainly settled into a routine here.#$e#It would be nice to shake things up sometime.$s",
	"Neutral_9": "You know what I haven't done in a while? A jigsaw puzzle. Maybe I'll get one...",
		
	"Bad_0": "It feels like we're just not on the same frequency lately.$s",
	"Bad_1": "*sigh*... I'm starting to like being at the clinic better than being at home.$s",
	"Bad_2": "Maybe you could cook your own dinner tonight for a change, @.$a",
	"Bad_3": "I feel like I must have done something wrong. You'd tell me if I had, right?$s",
	"Bad_4": "How long has it been since we sat down and talked?",
	"Bad_5": "Sometimes I worry you're out of the house so much just to avoid being around me.$s",
	"Bad_6": "I still feel like something's missing in my life...$s#$e#maybe you aren't what I needed after all.$s",
	"Bad_7": "Lately I feel like all I do is cook and clean.$s",
	"Bad_8": "Are you getting bored of me?$s",
	"Bad_9": "Do you think we made the right choice, getting married? Sometimes I wonder.$s",
	
	//Seasonal Marriage Dialogue - Spring
	//A lot of this is the default since I didn't want to get rid of them entirely; it changes in other seasons
	
	"Spring.Rainy_Day_0": "Spring rain is my favorite kind. It makes everything feel so fresh afterward.$h",
	"Spring.Rainy_Day_1": "It was so incredibly lonely living above the clinic by myself... I'm much happier now.$h",
	"Spring.Rainy_Day_2": "I woke up early, but I made sure not to wake you. You looked so peaceful.",
	"Spring.Rainy_Day_3": "I don't mind the rain. Sure, I can't watch the planes go by, but I can still listen to the radio chatter.#$e#It makes the whole thing a little more mysterious.",
	"Spring.Rainy_Day_4": "This is perfect weather for staying inside and reading the latest issue of \"Vascular Monthly\".#$e#It's more fun than it sounds!$h",
	"Spring.Rainy_Night_0": "How was your day, @? I caught up on some chores I wanted to get done.",
	"Spring.Rainy_Night_1": "I took the day to check if there were any leaks.#$b#This place is water-tight! Robin did an incredible job fixing it up.$h",
	"Spring.Rainy_Night_2": "You look a little soggy, @.#$b#Still refusing to use an umbrella, huh?$h",
	"Spring.Rainy_Night_3": "I always feel like I sleep better on rainy nights.#$b#The sound is incredibly soothing.",
	"Spring.Rainy_Night_4": "I made us a nice healthy dinner. Only fresh, wholesome ingredients from the valley. [225 226 237 196 200]$h#$e#It's so nice having more time to cook.",
	
	"Spring.Indoor_Day_0": "I think we're all striving to reach some kind of balance in life. Homeostasis, you know?#$e#For me, moving here was exactly what my body needed to find that balance.$l",
	"Spring.Indoor_Day_1": "Good morning, @! I made you a nutritious breakfast.[201]#$e#You're always so hard at work; you need your energy!$h",
	"Spring.Indoor_Day_2": "I'm going to study the medical literature today. It's important for me to keep up-to-date; new discoveries are made all the time.",
	"Spring.Indoor_Day_3": "I'm going to listen to some jazz music and finalize my medical reports today. What do you have planned, @?",
	"Spring.Indoor_Day_4": "I was afraid of you when we first met. It's funny to think about now that we've come so far.$h",
	"Spring.Indoor_Night_0": "You look like you could use a good massage tonight, @.#$e#Luckily I spent the day brushing up on my understanding of the muscular system.",
	"Spring.Indoor_Night_1": "I took it easy today... spent some time reading, fiddled with my radio, and worked on a model airplane.#$e#I feel like I've become much better at taking breaks since I married you.$h",
	"Spring.Indoor_Night_2": "I hope you know that I don't mind if you stay out late occasionally.#$e#I know you have a lot to get done every day.",
	"Spring.Indoor_Night_3": "It's really great to live somewhere as relaxing as %farm Farm.#$e#I feel like my blood pressure's improved significantly since I moved out here.$h",
	"Spring.Indoor_Night_4": "Oh! Sorry, I was just daydreaming and forgot what I was going to do.#$e#About what? Oh... You know. Planes.$l",
		
	"Spring.Outdoor_0": "The view from here is lovely. You've really done a great job with the place.$h",
	"Spring.Outdoor_1": "It's good to stop working and breathe in the fresh %farm Farm air sometimes. Don't you think?",
	"Spring.Outdoor_2": "I may not be the most exciting guy, but I'll stay loyal to you for the rest of my life.$l",
	"Spring.Outdoor_3": "@... you mean the world to me.$l",
	"Spring.Outdoor_4": "Watching your crops grow has made me want to learn more about the science behind farming. It's more complicated than I thought!",
	"Spring.Patio.1": "You know, \"The Journal of Tendon Dynamics\" is actually bearable when I'm reading out here.",
	"Spring.Patio.2": "I know it's not quite as impressive as your farm, but I've grown to really enjoy tending my little garden.$h",
	"Spring.Patio.3": "I've started reading for pleasure more. It's nice to put down the medical literature sometimes.",
	"Spring.Patio.4": "I was thinking about planting some herbs. It would be nice to have fresh basil for homemade pesto.",
		
	"Spring.funLeave.1": "I think I'll go out and get some fresh air today. It'll be nice to get out of the house.",
	"Spring.funLeave.2": "Oh, @! I was thinking of going out today. The valley is so nice this time of year.$h",
	"Spring.funLeave.3": "One of these days I'd like to work up to real hiking.#$b#For now, though, going into town is a good start.",
	"Spring.funReturn.1": "I had a nice day. Spending time alone now and then allows me to organize my thoughts.",
	"Spring.funReturn.2": "Did you have a good day, @?#$e#I'm a little tired, but the good kind of tired.",
	"Spring.funReturn.3": "I saw a rare Southern Valley Mallard on my walk today!$h#$b#I wish I'd had a camera with me to take a picture. I did manage to pick up a feather, though. [444]",
	
	"Spring.OneKid_0": "I always dreamed of having a family, you know.#$e#I used to think I'd be a bachelor forever... I love you so much.$l",
	"Spring.OneKid_1": "I'm not actually that worried about %kid1 getting hurt out on the farm.#$b#One of the best things about kids is how sturdy they are. They're built to get into trouble.$h",
	"Spring.TwoKids_0": "I believe a child should be allowed to play and explore to their heart's content. It's good to encourage their natural curiosity.",
	"Spring.TwoKids_1": "Keeping track of two children is better exercise than anything else I've ever tried!$h",
		
	//Seasonal Marriage Dialogue - Summer
	
	"Summer.Rainy_Day_0": "Take care that you don't slip in the mud outside!#$e#I can't help but worry about you.",
	"Summer.Rainy_Day_1": "This feels like a good day to stay in and work on one of my model planes.",
	"Summer.Rainy_Day_2": "Hm... I was going to go for a walk today, but that might not be in the cards.",
	"Summer.Rainy_Day_3": "If we're lucky, this rain will help cool things off a little.",
	"Summer.Rainy_Day_4": "I think I'll catch up on my reading today. I just got the latest issue of \"Head, Shoulders, Knees and Toes\".",
	"Summer.Rainy_Night_0": "Hi, @. Did you have a productive day today?#$e#I bet the rain didn't slow you down at all.$h",
	"Summer.Rainy_Night_1": "I've been hearing scratching coming from under the porch at night.#$b#Do you think we might have raccoons?",
	"Summer.Rainy_Night_2": "I never thought of myself as the \"rustic cabin\" kind of guy, but I've really taken a liking to it.$h",
	"Summer.Rainy_Night_3": "Try not to track any mud inside, @. I just mopped earlier.",
	"Summer.Rainy_Night_4": "You look hungry, @. Lucky for you, I decided to spend my day trying out a new recipe. [212 214 209 204]$h",
		
	"Summer.Indoor_Day_0": "The sky looks great today... so clear!#$e#From now on, I'm only going to go into the clinic when I have appointments. Otherwise I can just work from home!",
	"Summer.Indoor_Day_1": "Good morning, @! I got up early to make you breakfast.[201]#$e#I hope me banging around in the kitchen didn't wake you up.",
	"Summer.Indoor_Day_2": "Hm... what should I do today?#$e#Honestly, this heat makes me want to take a nap.$h",
	"Summer.Indoor_Day_3": "I've been thinking... maybe I'll try iced coffee for a change.#$e#Variety is the spice of life, right?$h",
	"Summer.Indoor_Day_4": "Days tend to be longest in Summer.#$b#That means more time to do whatever you like!#h",
	"Summer.Indoor_Night_0": "I find most of the Summer bugs annoying, but I have to admit, the butterflies are nice.",
	"Summer.Indoor_Night_1": "It's great living out here where there's relatively little light pollution.#$e#You can see almost every star in the sky.$l",
	"Summer.Indoor_Night_2": "This house has surprisingly good acoustics.#$b#It's almost got me thinking about picking up the piano again.",
	"Summer.Indoor_Night_3": "Are there really animate skeletons in the mines?#$e#You know, in retrospect, I shouldn't have asked.$s",
	"Summer.Indoor_Night_4": "...$l#$b#Oh, sorry. I just got caught up in looking at you.",
		
	"Summer.Outdoor_0": "Whoof... it's hot out here. I might head inside again soon.",
	"Summer.Outdoor_1": "I can't tell you how lucky I feel to get to spend my life with you.$l",
	"Summer.Outdoor_2": "Have you noticed? There's a bird's nest up under the roof.#$e#%farm Farm is so full of life!$h",
	"Summer.Outdoor_3": "This is so much nicer than being cooped up in the clinic all day.$l#$e#I love watching you work on the farm... hehe.$l",
	"Summer.Outdoor_4": "Be sure to drink enough water today, @. It's easy to get dehydrated in weather like this.",
	"Summer.Patio.1": "A bee landed on me earlier.#$b#Oh, don't worry! They don't sting unless you bother them. She went on her way eventually.$h",
	"Summer.Patio.2": "I might be overwatering my plants... I'm just worried about this heat drying them out!",
	"Summer.Patio.3": "I saw a rabbit past the fence not too long ago.#$b#If you're quiet he might come back.",
	"Summer.Patio.4": "Sometimes I think about bringing my radio equipment out here... but I'd just have to cart it back inside any time it rained.",
		
	"Summer.funLeave.1": "I'm putting down the paperwork today and going out. I could use some time to myself.",
	"Summer.funLeave.2": "I think I need to stretch my legs. I'll be back tonight, okay?",
	"Summer.funLeave.3": "I'm going out today, @. I'll let you know if I see any interesting wildlife!",
	"Summer.funReturn.1": "I've heard this can be used to make an excellent risotto. I'd love to try making one sometime. [259 248]",
	"Summer.funReturn.2": "I think I may have got a little bit of a sunburn, despite my best efforts... do my ears look red to you?",
	"Summer.funReturn.3": "Sometimes I think I should get one of those mobile casette players.#$b#It would be nice to listen to music while I'm out walking.",
	
	"Summer.OneKid_0": "I've found that a couple of minutes of some quiet jazz music puts %kid1 straight to sleep.#$b#I'm just glad something works reliably.$h",
	"Summer.OneKid_1": "%kid1 almost yanked out a chunk of my mustache earlier.#$b#A strong grip is a good sign! It means motor development is proceeding at a healthy rate.",
	"Summer.TwoKids_0": "I wonder if the kids are old enough to go out and catch fireflies...#$e#Oh, we'd set them free, of course. But they're fun to look at for a little while.",
	"Summer.TwoKids_1": "%kid1 helped me make fruit juice popsicles yesterday.#$e#Well. I made the popsicles. %kid1 mostly handled eating them.$h",
	
	//Seasonal Dialogue - Fall
	
	"Fall.Rainy_Day_0": "Do you ever think about how the older we get, the faster time seems to go by?#$b#Ah, sorry. Days like this make me more contemplative than normal.",
	"Fall.Rainy_Day_1": "The sound of the rain is almost like a natural drumline.#$b#I wonder what nature's equivalent to a saxophone is...?",
	"Fall.Rainy_Day_2": "They're playing classic movies all day today on TV. I might see if \"The Zuzu City Express\" is on.",
	"Fall.Rainy_Day_3": "You don't need to do any watering today, so why don't you stay in this morning?#$e#It would be nice to just sit and talk for a bit.",
	"Fall.Rainy_Day_4": "I've heard that pumpkin flavored coffee is popular this time of year.#$e#I admit it does sound interesting...",
	"Fall.Rainy_Night_0": "I spent today re-organizing the kitchen cabinets.#$e#I know it sounds boring, but I find that kind of thing relaxing. I can just put on some music and turn my brain off.",
	"Fall.Rainy_Night_1": "I think the small moments in life are just as important as the big ones.#$e#Just being here with you and listening to the rain is enough for me.",
	"Fall.Rainy_Night_2": "Wow, is it %time already? Today just flew by.#$e#I guess I must have been having fun.$h",
	"Fall.Rainy_Night_3": "Hi. It's good to see you.$h#$e#Oh, me? I spent the day skimming through some medical journals.",
	"Fall.Rainy_Night_4": "I decided to finally try out one of those recipes I had saved. I think it came out alright, but you tell me what you think. [230 235 236 237]$h",
		
	"Fall.Indoor_Day_0": "Good morning, @. I've been up for a while already.#$e#Sometimes it's nice to enjoy the early morning quiet.",
	"Fall.Indoor_Day_1": "Here's your breakfast, @, just how you like it. I think I got the consistency on the eggs perfect this time. [201]$h",
	"Fall.Indoor_Day_2": "If you see any edible mushrooms while you're out today, be sure to pick them up.#$e#There's nothing fresher than straight off the ground!$h", 
	"Fall.Indoor_Day_3": "Sometimes I wonder what my life would be like if you'd never read that letter from your Grandfather...#$b#I'm glad that you did.$l",
	"Fall.Indoor_Day_4": "Did you sleep well last night, @? I had the strangest dream...#$e#You were growing pumpkins, but they just kept growing until they were taller than I was! Weird, right?",
	"Fall.Indoor_Night_0": "You know, there are so many good fishing spots in Pelican Town but I've never actually gone fishing.#$e#We should make a day of it sometime. Would you like that?",
	"Fall.Indoor_Night_1": "I think there's an owl living in the woods around here.#$e#I've heard hooting at night before, but I've never managed to spot it.",
	"Fall.Indoor_Night_2": "I didn't pick up any radio chatter today, but I did see several flocks of birds heading South.",
	"Fall.Indoor_Night_3": "I'm due for an eye exam but I've been putting off scheduling one.#$b#They say doctors are the worst patients and I admit there's some truth to that.",
	"Fall.Indoor_Night_4": "It's funny to think about how I used to be scared of getting old.#$b#I think what I was really scared of was getting old alone. I'd love to grow old with you.$l",
		
	"Fall.Outdoor_0": "This is a very safe spot. You go on ahead and take care of business, don't worry about me.",
	"Fall.Outdoor_1": "Are you thinking of decorating for Spirit's Eve?#$e#I never did when I lived alone, but then, there wasn't much point.",
	"Fall.Outdoor_2": "You know, Fall foliage is only so colorful because all of the leaves are dying. It feels bittersweet, doesn't it?",
	"Fall.Outdoor_3": "Crisp fall air... a hot cup of coffee... I can't imagine what else I could ask for.$h",
	"Fall.Outdoor_4": "I've grown very fond of %farm Farm. I wouldn't want to live anywhere else.",
	"Fall.Patio.1": "These mushrooms are purely decorative. They're pretty, but no good for eating!",
	"Fall.Patio.2": "It's a little chilly out here today. Maybe I should have worn thicker socks.",
	"Fall.Patio.3": "Hm? Oh, sorry. I was completely caught up in this book. I've been on a historical fiction kick lately.",
	"Fall.Patio.4": "I should ask Leah to build me one of those decorative windmills.#$b#I think it would look nice out here, don't you?",
		
	"Fall.funLeave.1": "I think I'll go out today. There's something uniquely refreshing about crisp Fall air.",
	"Fall.funLeave.2": "I'm going to be out of the house today, so don't worry if you come back and I'm not here.",
	"Fall.funLeave.3": "I have some things I'd like to take care of in town. See you tonight?",
	"Fall.funReturn.1": "I happened to come across a wild mushroom on my walk today. A few more of these and we could make a great pasta sauce. [257 281 404 430]",
	"Fall.funReturn.2": "I know it's a little childish, but I do sometimes go out of my way to step on dry leaves.#$e#That sound is one of the best parts of Fall.$h",
	"Fall.funReturn.3": "I saw the strangest thing today: a mushroom as tall as a tree.#$e#I didn't know they could get that big. It was a little intimidating.",
	
	"Fall.OneKid_0": "Don't worry about %kid1; I'll handle parenting duties today. You can focus on getting things done around the farm.",
	"Fall.OneKid_1": "I suppose now that I have a child I'll have to warm up to Spirit's Eve.#$b#If %kid1 wants to go through the maze, though, that's all you.",
	"Fall.TwoKids_0": "The house is really starting to feel full now with both %kid1 and %kid2 here.#$e#I like it; it's cozy.",
	"Fall.TwoKids_1": "I think %kid1 and %kid2 are really bonding as siblings. I saw the two of them reading a book together earlier.#$e#Well. Looking at the pictures in a book, anyway. Close enough.",
	
	//Seasonal Dialogue - Winter
	//I believe some of these don't actually proc in winter, but I'm leaving them in anyway. Secret dialogue! If you're reading this file, hello, I hope you're having a good day. I just finished my last grad school class of the semester and I am feeling Grand :)
	
	"Winter.Rainy_Day_0": "It's a little unusual for it to rain in Winter. I wonder if Spring is coming early this year?",
	"Winter.Rainy_Day_1": "Make sure you stay dry today, @. I don't want you to become hypothermic.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Day_2": "There was some interesting chatter over the radio this morning.#$b#Apparently an Ember Airlines pilot had to make an emergency water landing.#$b#It was all anyone could talk about.$h",
	"Winter.Rainy_Day_3": "How would you feel about soup for dinner tonight? This feels like soup weather.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Day_4": "Have you got your flu shot yet, @? It's best to do it sooner rather than later.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Night_0": "Do they make heated weighted blankets?#$e#If they don't, they should. There must be a market for that.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Night_1": "I checked the smoke detectors today.#$b#If we're going to have a fire going we should make sure that they're all functional.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Night_2": "You look a little chilled, @.#$b#Go and warm yourself up by the fire, alright? I'll make you something warm to drink.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Night_3": "Hm... I wonder what gift I ought to get Maru this year.#$b#If she wants something she tends to just make it herself, so she's hard to shop for.",
	"Winter.Rainy_Night_4": "I've been thinking about getting into journaling.#$e#I've heard it's good for a person's mental health, but I think I'd worry too much about making it look nice.",
		
	"Winter.Indoor_Day_0": "Don't worry about getting me the perfect gift this year.#$b#I'd treasure anything you gave me.$l",
	"Winter.Indoor_Day_1": "Don't forget to eat a healthy breakfast, @. It's the best way to start your day! [201]$h",
	"Winter.Indoor_Day_2": "Every year Maru gifts me a coffee mug with a different element from the periodic table on it.#$e#I'm hoping this year I'll get the last of the Halogens.$h",
	"Winter.Indoor_Day_3": "I mixed hot cocoa powder into my coffee this morning. It's a very lazy way to make a mocha!$h",
	"Winter.Indoor_Day_4": "I'm going to do laundry today. If you have anything you want washed, this is your last chance to put it in the hamper.",
	"Winter.Indoor_Night_0": "You're as ${handsome^beautiful^perfect}$ as the day I married you.$l#$e#Too cheesy? Sorry, I get a little sentimental this time of year.",
	"Winter.Indoor_Night_1": "I decided to go a little bit out of my comfort zone and try reading a mystery book.#$e#Did you know there's an entire genre called \"cozy mystery\"? It sounds contradictory but I'm actually enjoying it a lot!$h",
	"Winter.Indoor_Night_2": "Maru once tried to explain something called \"Flight Simulator\" to me.#$b#I've never been fantastic with computers, but I might look into it.",
	"Winter.Indoor_Night_3": "Don't forget to leave the taps running overnight to keep the pipes from freezing.#$e#I made that mistake once. Trust me.$s",
	"Winter.Indoor_Night_4": "Did you hear? The Zuzu Underground Orchestra is releasing a new album this month.#$e#This will be the first one with the new cellist. We'll see how it turns out.",
		
	"Winter.Outdoor_0": "Being able to see my own breath is always fun...$h#$b#Right up until it fogs up my glasses.$a",
	"Winter.Outdoor_1": "They've started playing holiday music on all of the radio stations.#$e#I don't mind it as much as other people, but it's still nice to take a break from it out here where it's quiet.",
	"Winter.Outdoor_2": "You can still get sunburnt in the Winter, you know. Protecting your skin is a year-round job.",
	"Winter.Outdoor_3": "Are you planning out how you're going to organize your crops this Spring?#$b#Or are you going to play it by ear?",
	"Winter.Outdoor_4": "Oh, good morning, @. I was just enjoying the brisk morning air.",
	"Winter.Patio.1": "I'm taking the Winter break to decide what I want to plant out here come Spring.#$e#I was thinking tulips might be nice.",
	"Winter.Patio.2": "Hm... maybe I should ask Robin to build a roof over this patio.#$e#Then I could sit out here even in the snow or the rain.",
	"Winter.Patio.3": "The book I'm reading is set in a desert country.#$b#It's my theory that reading about a place where it's hot might fool my brain into thinking it's warm here too.#$e#There's no real science behind that, but hope springs eternal.$h",
	"Winter.Patio.4": "Hi, @. Where are you headed today?#$e#Don't stay out too late. We're supposed to hit sub-zero temperatures tonight.", 
		
	"Winter.funLeave.1": "Alright... time to bundle up and run some errands. Do you need anything in town, @?",
	"Winter.funLeave.2": "Hm... we could use some more hand soap. I can go pick some up.#$e#Proper hand-washing is essential in the middle of cold and flu season.",
	"Winter.funLeave.3": "I think it might be nice to get out of the house today.#$b#I feel like I'm starting to get cabin fever.",
	"Winter.funReturn.1": "I tripped over this on my way home... it was hidden under the snow. [412 416 536 709 749]#$e#It looked like something you could use.$h",
	"Winter.funReturn.2": "Phew! It's good to be home. What did you do today?#$e#Did you spend all day in the mines again?#h",
	"Winter.funReturn.3": "Sorry I'm back a little late; I kept getting distracted.#$b#Oh, not by anything important. Mainly watching the birds.",
	
	"Winter.OneKid_0": "It just ocurred to me that having a child means we can officially start establishing family holiday traditions.#$e#I'll have to think of some...",
	"Winter.OneKid_1": "Did you want to do family postcards this year?#$e#I have some far-off relatives who I'm sure would love an update on how %kid1 is doing.",
	"Winter.TwoKids_0": "%kid1 took a drink of my coffee earlier before I could take the cup away.#$b#I think that what's called a 'teaching moment'. There's a reason only grown-ups drink coffee.$h",
	"Winter.TwoKids_1": "It's interesting how quickly children form distinct personalities.#$e#%kid1 and %kid2 are totally different, wouldn't you say?",
	
	//Misc
	
	"Killed.1": "Easy now. Take it slow.",
	"Killed.2": "You were found unconscious and in critical condition; there was no time to transport you to Zuzu City.#$b#I had to intervene to stabilize you.$s",
	"Killed.3": "You can stay here in the clinic until you get your feet back under you.",
	"Killed.4": "#Just be more careful out there, for my sake?#$b# I know I sometimes worry too much, but when this kind of thing happens it makes it difficult not to.$s#$b# I don't know what I'd do if I ever lost you.|I know it's tempting, but don't head right back out there once you leave. At least get a night's rest first.",
	
	"Rainy.1": "Hi @! It's good weather for staying inside and reading.#$e#So... have you read anything good lately?",
	"Rainy.2": "Have you ever noticed that almost no one in this town uses an umbrella?#$e#I think I saw Sebastian with one, once...$s",
	"Rainy.3": "I suppose it's nice to have a day off from watering your crops.#$b#Everyone needs a break now and then.$h",
	"Rainy.4": "I hate going outside on days like this.#$b#My glasses get all fogged up and then I'm as blind with them on as I am without.",
	"Rainy.5": "Ugh. I stepped in a puddle earlier and my socks are still soaked.$s",
	"Rainy.6": "Wearing wet clothing can't actually make you sick, but I'd still recommend changing when you get home.#$b#Basic comfort is also important!",
	
}
